  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "建築設計(一)",
    "sub_ename": "ARCHITECTURAL DESIGN(1)",
    "describe_ch": "本課程為建築的基本設計入門，介紹建築設計的基本元素與組合原理，尤其著重光、影、造型、空間與材料的呈現和設計概念的操作技巧，同時將設計概念完整呈現於2-D版面與立體模型。訓練學生設計作品能綜合理性、知性與感性於思考及創作的過程中。",
    "describe_eh": "This is the introduction course in architectural design. The aim of the course is to introduce fundamental knowledge of design elements and principles, particular emphasis on light and shadow, form and space, and materials. Modeling making is also part of the design training, because the conceptual approach might be discovered through the making and creating process. The result of the course is the ability to represent the design concept and idea graphically in 2-dimension and translate into a quality 3-dimensional model at the end of first semester. It is also the central core of the course to think and create rationally, intellectually, and sensationally.",
    "pre_subname": "",
    "pre_sub_id3": null,
    "pre_sub_ename": "",
    "pre_describe": null,
    "pre_describe_en": null,
    "scr_credit": 4.0
  },
